                            <comment id="15376703" author="eolivelli" created="Thu, 14 Jul 2016 09:58:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The fix is quite simple, but I have only one doubt, in BookKeeperAdmin:LedgerEntriesIterator&lt;br/&gt;
old code is&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;@Override
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; LedgerEntry next() {            
            ++nextEntryId;
            LedgerEntry entry = currentEntry;
            currentEntry = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;;
            &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; entry;
        }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;my proposal is&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;@Override
        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;public&lt;/span&gt; LedgerEntry next() {
            &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (lastEntryId &amp;gt; -1 &amp;amp;&amp;amp; nextEntryId &amp;gt; lastEntryId) {
                &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; NoSuchElementException();
            }
            ++nextEntryId;
            LedgerEntry entry = currentEntry;
            currentEntry = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;;
            &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; entry;
        }
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;FindBugs complaints that a call to &quot;next()&quot; will never throw NoSuchElementException.&lt;br/&gt;
The logic of this iterator is not very clear to me in case of lastEntryId = -1&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The proposed fix adds the throw statement for a sure NoSuchElementException case, but leaves uncovered the lastEntryId = -1 case.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
